  "title": "Nepal-Tibet Flash Floods and Himalayan Ice Collapse",
  "summary": "A flash flood in Nepal and a landslide in Upper Subansiri district resulted in five Army personnel missing and four people dead, while a similar event in Tibet saw 469 deaths in Nepal and three in Tibet. The floods highlighted the devastating effects of rapid melting of Himalayan ice.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "A flash flood in Arunachal Pradesh and a major landslide at a road construction site in Upper Subansiri district resulted in five Army personnel missing and four people dead.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "A collapsed Himalayan glacier caused devastating floods, highlighting the issue of Himalayan ice melting.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The floods led to at least 93,000 'in great need' people being affected, with three additional Australians confirmed missing overnight.",
