      "title": "Controversial plans for a Daniel Andrews sculpture officially scrapped by Victorian government",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/29/controversial-plans-for-a-daniel-andrews-sculpture-officially-scrapped-by-victorian-government",
      "description": "<p>The $134,000 cost of the statue of the former Victorian premier has been heavily criticised by the Liberal opposition</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The Carroll government in Victoria has cancelled controversial plans for a statue of former Labor premier Daniel Andrews.</p><p>Work began in May on the statue commemorating the former premier’s more than 3,000 days in office, as part of a 1999 policy recognising long-serving Victorian premiers.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/29/controversial-plans-for-a-daniel-andrews-sculpture-officially-scrapped-by-victorian-government\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-28T23:47:37"
    },
    {
      "title": "Number of Australians missing in Nepal’s deadly floods rises again, as Albanese deploys more personnel",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/29/australians-missing-nepal-floods-total-rises-albanese-dfat-personnel-arriving",
      "description": "<p>There are now 41 Australians missing, and four rapid response team members are expected to arrive in Kathmandu</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/28/nepal-tibet-flash-floods-red-cross-rescuers-death-toll\">At least 93,000 ‘in great need’ after Nepal-Tibet flash floods</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/27/nepal-tibet-flash-flood-visual-guide-why-how-flooding-happened-floods-cause-reason-explained\">How the deadly Nepal and Tibet flash flood unfolded – a visual guide</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The number of Australians who were reported missing in the catastrophic Nepal flooding disaster has risen to 41, as one family celebrates after an unaccounted-for woman made contact with them yesterday.</p><p>It means three additional Australians were confirmed missing overnight – up from 38 who remained unaccounted for on Friday evening.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/29/australians-missing-nepal-floods-total-rises-albanese-dfat-personnel-arriving\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-28T22:53:57"
    }
